# URL of the Cloudflare Worker registration endpoint.
# Copy this file to .env and set the value for your environment.
# In production this is set in your deployment environment (e.g. Cloudflare Pages).
PUBLIC_WORKER_URL=https://alleyadmin-registration-worker.jshprintz.workers.dev

# ── Analytics ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set to 1 to require consent before any analytics event is sent. When
# enabled, an unanswered banner counts as a decline, and the choice is
# recorded in the `analytics-consent` cookie which the Pages Function reads.
#
# Now 1. The Zaraz Consent Management platform is enabled on the
# alleyadmin.app zone with an "Analytics" purpose assigned to the GA4 tool,
# and `initAnalyticsConsentBridge` in src/lib/analytics-client.ts mirrors the
# visitor's choice from that modal into the `analytics-consent` cookie.
# Verified in production in both directions: Accept All writes 'granted' and
# loads GA4, Reject All writes 'denied' and loads nothing.
PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_REQUIRE_CONSENT=1

# ── Pages Function environment (NOT Astro) ───────────────────────────
# The variables below are read by functions/api/analytics/event.ts at runtime
# and are NOT part of the client bundle, so they carry no PUBLIC_ prefix. Set
# them in the Cloudflare dashboard under Workers & Pages > alley-admin >
# Settings > Environment variables. They are listed here for documentation
# only; adding them to a local .env does nothing.
#
#   ANALYTICS_GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID   G-P73EZX3K69
#   ANALYTICS_GA4_API_SECRET       encrypt this one — it is a credential
#   ANALYTICS_REQUIRE_CONSENT      mirror of PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_REQUIRE_CONSENT
#
# ANALYTICS_REQUIRE_CONSENT must be set to 1 in the dashboard alongside this
# file's change. The two are independent: this one gates the browser before it
# calls the endpoint, that one gates the endpoint itself. Setting only one
# leaves the other path ungated.
#
# The API secret is NOT the gtag.js snippet. Create one under
# GA4 Admin > Data streams > (stream) > Measurement Protocol API secrets.
# If either value is missing the endpoint returns ok without delivering,
# which is the intended state until they are provisioned.
#
# This endpoint is only a fallback for visitors whose browser did not load
# Zaraz. Zaraz is configured on the alleyadmin.app zone with the same GA4
# measurement ID and handles the normal path — that configuration lives in the
# Cloudflare dashboard, not in this repository.
